Theorem IC-2: Interprocedural contract rule signatures — IC-1 through IC-7 + IC-8a + IC-8 confirmation-of-removal

  Preconditions:
    - Interprocedural contracts are the per-function MemoryContract summary
      computed via SCC fixpoint per Annex E §AIMS
    - Step 1 of the AIMS pipeline (analyze_program) runs this analysis
      per Annex E §AIMS §6 (interprocedural-first)
    - Convergence depends on monotone componentwise max + finite domain
      per IC-7
    - 8 active IC rules + 1 IC-8a address-taken / closure rule govern
      SCC decomposition / contract initialization / fixpoint / return /
      effect / FIP / convergence / address-taken-init
    - IC-8 was REMOVED from Annex E §AIMS (same root cause as DP-10)

  Soundness property:
    IC-1 (SCC decomposition + topological ordering):
      type : CallGraph -> List (List FunctionId)
      call graph decomposed into SCCs; processed in topological order
      (callees before callers).

    IC-2 (ParamContract initialization at most-optimistic state):
      type : FunctionId -> List ParamContract
      each parameter initializes (B, empty, absent, bl, u, may_share=false);
      fixpoint promotes toward conservative.

    IC-3 (ParamContract componentwise max join + may_share OR):
      type : List ParamContract -> List ParamContract
      iterate until no dim changes; access(max), consumption(max),
      cardinality(max), locality(max), uniqueness(max), may_share(OR).

    IC-4 (ReturnContract per-dim join over return paths):
      type : List ReturnContract -> ReturnContract
      uniqueness(join), preserves_freshness(AND), locality(join), shape(join);
      freshness requires ALL paths preserve.

    IC-5 (EffectSummary derivation):
      type : FunctionId -> EffectSummary
      derived from instruction stream + callee contracts per Annex E §AIMS
      IC-5 procedure (7-field OR-join over instructions; NOT joined from
      per-variable EffectClass per §AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note).

    IC-6 (FipContract sum-type tier join):
      type : List FipContract -> FipContract
      Never absorbs all; Conditional absorbs Bounded / Certified;
      Bounded(n) join Bounded(m) = Bounded(max(n, m));
      Certified IFF zero unmatched alloc / dealloc in realized IR;
      timing POST-REALIZATION (step 5a).

    IC-7 (convergence iteration limit):
      type : FunctionId -> Int
      iteration limit = param_count x 13 + 8 + 6 + 4
        (param=13, return=8, EffectSummary=6, ContextBehavior=4);
      FipContract excluded (post-realization);
      on exceeded -> widen all to most conservative + emit diagnostic.

    IC-8a (address-taken / closure non-enumerable call sites):
      type : FunctionId -> List ParamContract
      address-taken / closures with non-enumerable call sites SHALL
      initialize parameters CONSERVATIVE:
        (O, U, omega, top, ms, may_share=true)
      closures with known call sites (immediately-invoked / single-use)
      participate normally.

    IC-8 confirmation-of-removal entry:

      IC-8 — Parameter-uniqueness from caller-consumption (REMOVED)

      Removed in: Annex E §AIMS IC-8 removal note
        (same root cause as DP-10)

      Root cause: a caller with a MaybeShared argument used linearly may
        still carry multiple logical owner credits through upstream aliases;
        deriving callee parameter uniqueness from caller consumption patterns
        was unsound.

      Subsumed by: IC-2 + IC-3 SCC fixpoint as natural convergence
        (parameter uniqueness established by joined caller-side state,
        not by inference from caller consumption patterns).

      No theorem skeleton to discharge; this is a CONFIRMATION entry only.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-06 interprocedural contract proofs
            (8 active theorems: IC-1, IC-2, IC-3, IC-4, IC-5, IC-6, IC-7,
            IC-8a + IC-8 confirmation entry)

    Engines dispatched:
      fixpoint (IC-3 + IC-4 + IC-5 monotone fixpoint convergence)
      interprocedural_summary (SCC topological ordering + per-function
                               contract composition)
      case_analysis (IC-6 FipContract 4-tier join + IC-8a closure
                     non-enumerable detection)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-06 discharges per-rule IC proofs
